# Massive refresh-randomized local cream

Status: COMPLETED
Milestone: M58 Local-only varied large clumps and refined pointer trail
Dependencies: 62_CATALOGUE_ONLY_RIGHT_PAGE_TAGS.todo, 64_ENTRANCE_NEON_ICONS.todo

## Purpose

After finishing the public website work, update http://127.0.0.1:4174/ with
massive connected cream clumps mixed with smaller clumps. Randomize initial
quantity and sizes on each refresh. Make the pointer blob smaller and its actual
visible trail slightly longer.

## Tasks

- [x] Finish the current website work before implementing this local follow-up.
- [x] Preserve current local source and verify independent offline-export behavior.
- [x] Introduce bounded refresh randomness, stable within each load and resize.
- [x] Keep large/small clumps connected internally without one continuous smear.
- [x] Reduce the pointer head; measure the longer visible trail rather than a constant.
- [x] Exercise seeds, viewports, placement limits, fallbacks and lifecycle behavior.
- [x] Record local completion without publishing experimental files.

## Acceptance criteria

- Some clearly massive clumps and smaller clumps; varied size and quantity on refresh.
- Original cream shading, center etched frost and side pattern behind cream retained.
- Composition remains stable while moving or resizing; safe GPU and placement bounds.
- Cursor stays responsive, visibly smaller, with a slightly longer bounded trail.
- Pause, reduced motion, no-JavaScript and graphics failure paths remain usable.
- No production integration, image-tool review or Instagram posting.

